SUMMARY:Nuestros Parques: Let's Climb A Mountain!
DESCRIPTION:Bilingual hikes and community events for the whole family! \nProgram Location:\nTaylor Mountain Regional Park and Preserve \nMeeting Place:\nKawana Terrace Rd. Entrance\, Parking Lot \nJoin us for a bilingual hike exploring the park’s unique natural and cultural features. This hike is moderately challenging\, with some steep sections. Strollers are not recommended\, and small children may find parts of the trail difficult. Bring your lunch to enjoy a relaxed group picnic together. Se habla español. Registration is encouraged but not required. \nPlease bring your own water and snacks. We recommend participants dress in layers and bring a hat and sunscreen. Most programs will happen rain or shine\, but may be canceled during heavy rains\, heavy smoke\, or extreme temperatures. Please let us know ahead of time if you have accessibility needs so we can best support your experience. Parking fees apply but are waived with a Regional Parks membership pass. For more information\, contact ParkPrograms@sonomacounty.gov
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/nuestros-parques-lets-climb-a-mountain/
LOCATION:Taylor Mountain Regional Park\, 3820 Petaluma Hill Road\, Santa Rosa\, CA
CATEGORIES:Recreation
GEO:38.4024;-122.693
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Taylor Mountain Regional Park 3820 Petaluma Hill Road Santa Rosa CA;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=3820 Petaluma Hill Road:geo:-122.693,38.4024
END:VEVENT
